    <bpmn:task id="task_qn28mwse" name="Recall &#38; latency bench" dai:notes="benches/recall.rs (Apple M4, 100k×128, 1k queries, k=10, defaults l_search=100). LATENCY MET everywhere: p99 ≤ 0.35 ms (target 10 ms). RECALL: low-rank (16-d latent) data PASS — cosine 1.000, euclidean 1.000, dot 0.958. i.i.d. Gaussian (literal &#39;random&#39; data) FAIL at l_search=100 — cosine 0.578, euclidean 0.745, dot 0.036. Full-rank random data is the known worst case for graph ANN (in-memory Vamana gives the same numbers, so it&#39;s not PQ/disk). At l_search=1000: cosine 0.994 / euclidean 0.963, p99 2.7 / 1.5 ms. i.i.d. dot stays poor (MIPS→L2 reduction limitation). Fixes made while benchmarking: (1) PQ split dims evenly — 129-d dot space with m=32 had ~6 all-padding sub-vectors; (2) inner-product ADC on original dims for dot (lowrank dot 0.78→0.92); (3) 64 max-norm entry points for dot search (→0.958). Needs a decision on the requirement wording / default l_search." dai:agentStatus="failed" dai:planRef="task_0nw81v9s">
      <bpmn:incoming>flow_f6pnn0jl</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>flow_wt0h15v4</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="flow_f6pnn0jl" sourceRef="task_tm9f7oms" targetRef="task_qn28mwse" />
